"""Independent open-book application questions; indices intentionally balanced."""
QUESTIONS=[]
def q(stem,options,answer,feedback):QUESTIONS.append(dict(question=stem,options=options,answer=answer,feedback=feedback))
q('A team verified the installed vessel against its accepted arrangement. Which conclusion is supported?', ['Every future batch will meet its mixing specification','The installed arrangement matches the reviewed scope','The cleaning process removes all relevant residues'],1,'Limit the conclusion to installation evidence; performance and cleaning need their own studies.')
q('Two inspectors used different revisions of the instrument schedule. What should happen?', ['Reconcile the controlled baseline and assess the affected checks','Combine both checklists without evaluating the differences','Select the revision with the greater number of passing results'],0,'A consistent applicable baseline is needed to interpret the observations.')
q('An equipment tag matches but the manufacturer serial differs from the schedule. What is justified?', ['Accept the vessel because the site tag is the primary identifier','Replace the schedule entry without investigating the difference','Resolve the identity discrepancy before relying on the match'],2,'A tag match does not resolve conflicting equipment identity.')
q('A drawing lacks the required removal clearance. How should a measured 300 mm be treated?', ['As a universal GMP minimum for maintenance access','As an observation whose acceptance criterion remains unresolved','As proof that the manufacturer removal envelope is satisfied'],1,'The observed distance cannot create its own criterion; no universal 300 mm limit is taught.')
q('A gasket certificate describes a lot that cannot be linked to the installed gasket. What remains open?', ['Traceability between the material evidence and installed item','The requirement to replace every metal contact component','The need to change all qualification stages to one protocol'],0,'The missing item-to-evidence link must be resolved through an applicable controlled approach.')
q('The installed material matches its specification. Which claim still needs separate evidence?', ['The compared material identifier matches the specification','The identity record relates to the inspected component','The cleaning process is effective for the intended residues'],2,'Matching material identity does not demonstrate cleaning effectiveness.')
q('A utility line is labelled correctly but connected to a different branch than the drawing specifies. What is appropriate?', ['Accept the label as sufficient evidence of correct installation','Record and investigate the connection discrepancy','Revise the drawing to match without an impact assessment'],1,'A label does not correct an incorrect or unassessed physical connection.')
q('A utility was qualified before a new vessel branch was added. What is needed for the extension?', ['Assessment of the change and applicable verification scope','Automatic acceptance under the original utility report','Only a new tag, because the utility source is unchanged'],0,'The extension must be evaluated; previous qualification does not automatically cover a changed system.')
q('Indication is 40.4 °C and reference is 40.0 °C. Which signed error and simple comparison are correct?', ['−0.4 °C; outside the fictional ±0.5 °C limit','+0.8 °C; outside the fictional ±0.5 °C limit','+0.4 °C; within the fictional ±0.5 °C limit'],2,'Indication minus reference is +0.4 °C. This arithmetic is not a complete uncertainty or acceptance decision.')
q('A current certificate has suitable range but identifies another instrument. What follows?', ['Use it because the range covers the planned test','Resolve certificate applicability to the installed instrument','Use it because both instruments came from one supplier'],1,'Identity, not just date and range, is necessary for applicability.')
q('An instrument is found outside its required calibration status after IQ measurements. What should be assessed?', ['Only the date needed on the next calibration label','Only whether the operator signed the original readings','The validity of affected measurements and required follow-up'],2,'A new calibration record alone does not establish the validity of earlier evidence.')
q('The control-system version is recorded during IQ. Which next step is still needed as applicable?', ['Validation of relevant functions and controls under the approved approach','Acceptance of all audit-trail behaviour from the version number','Acceptance of backup restoration from the version screenshot'],0,'Version identification does not demonstrate functional controls or complete Annex 11 compliance.')
q('A supplier manual covers a different installed model. What is the strongest response?', ['File it because the product family is broadly similar','Verify applicability and obtain the required correct instructions','Treat all maintenance requirements as not applicable'],1,'The handover needs instructions relevant to the installed model/configuration.')
q('A factory test is proposed for reuse after transport and site assembly. What supports reuse?', ['The supplier letterhead and an unchanged report title','The length of the original test report and number of signatures','Applicable controlled evidence and justified lack of relevant impact'],2,'Assess configuration, method, data and effects of transport/installation; retain required site checks.')
q('A photograph shows a readable nameplate but cannot be linked to any location or check. What is needed?', ['Context and an evidence reference connecting it to the inspected item','A higher pass percentage in the summary report','A replacement image without retaining the original record'],0,'An image needs a clear relationship to the relevant equipment and verification record.')
q('A serial number was transposed in a handwritten record. Which correction is appropriate?', ['Erase the entry and write the expected serial in its place','Preserve the original and make an attributed, dated correction','Rewrite the page and discard the page with the original entry'],1,'Follow the approved procedure, preserve the original information and record a reason where appropriate.')
q('A protocol check was not performed because access was unsafe. Which status is accurate?', ['Passed because the remaining equipment was satisfactory','Not applicable because inspection was inconvenient','Not checked, with the limitation and follow-up recorded'],2,'An incomplete check is distinct from a justified scope exclusion or a demonstrated pass.')
q('An installed valve differs from the accepted specification. Which route is defensible?', ['Document the discrepancy, assess impact and authorize correction or change','Edit the acceptance criterion to match the supplied valve','Close the check when the supplier confirms receipt of the complaint'],0,'A discrepancy requires an evidence-based controlled response and defined verification.')
q('Nine of ten checks are supported, but gasket traceability remains open. What does 90% mean?', ['Numerical coverage only; it does not authorize the next stage','Automatic OQ permission because it exceeds the practice target','Complete installation suitability if the missing record is promised'],0,'9/10 is 90%, but significance and activity-specific assessment govern the decision.')
q('A proposed dry OQ activity is unaffected by an open wetted-system finding. What supports conditional progression?', ['The project schedule and the supplier commitment to close the finding','The number of completed checks and the overall practice score','Documented no-significant-impact assessment and responsible authorization'],2,'Annex 15 §2.10 concerns a defined next-stage activity; the open finding is not automatically closed.')
